      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nInterested in this property? Sign up for mySherryFitz to arrange your viewing, see current offers, or make your own offer. Register now at SherryFitz.ie.\n\nSherry FitzGerald Reilly are delighted to present No. 19 Knightsfield Park, Dunsany, a beautifully presented three-bedroom semi-detached home which has been lovingly designed and maintained by its current owners. Presented in top condition throughout, this wonderful property offers a superb opportunity for those seeking a comfortable and stylish family home in a peaceful village setting.\n\nThe accommodation is complemented by a thoughtfully designed interior, creating a warm and welcoming atmosphere throughout. Every effort has been made by the current owners to create a home that is both attractive and practical, making it ready for its new owners to move in and enjoy.\n\nExternally, the property benefits from a large green area to the front, providing an attractive outlook and a pleasant open aspect. To the rear, a private garden offers an ideal space for outdoor dining, relaxing and entertaining, while the addition of a log cabin provides a versatile extra space which could be used as a home office, hobby room or simply a peaceful retreat. There is also full planning for an extension. \n\nKnightsfield Park enjoys a pleasant residential setting in the village of Dunsany, with the local national school and GAA facilities close by. The nearby town of Dunshaughlin offers a wider range of shops, cafés, schools and everyday amenities, while the surrounding towns of Trim and Navan are also within convenient reach. For commuters, the property benefits from access to the M3 motorway, providing a straightforward route towards Dublin, while local bus services offer additional transport options.\n\nCombining its excellent condition, attractive design, private garden and peaceful setting, No. 19 Knightsfield Park is sure to appeal to first-time buyers, families and those seeking a well-maintained home in the heart of County Meath."
      },
